

titre$Ceriporiopsis from East Russia
com$Maria Nunez, Erast Parmasto and Leif Ryvarden/ adapt GF 01/2014
rem$LANGUE$Anglais



1,0 $ Basidiospores cylindrical to allantoid, less than 1.5 µm wide $ C. subvermispora
1,2 $ Basidiospores subcylindrical to subglobose, wider than 1.5 µm 
1,0$source :///New and interesting polypores from East Russia///Fungal Diversity 6 107-114
2,3 $ Basidiospores shorter than 5 µm in longest dimension
2,6 $ Basidiospores longer than 5 µm in longest dimension
3,0 $ Pore surface becoming partly blackish when bruised or dried, basidiospores up to 3 µm long $ C. albonigrescens
3,4 $ Pore surface more or less unchanged when bruised or dry, basidiospores longer than 3 µm .
4,0 $ Basidiospores subcylindrical, 1.5-2 µm wide, basal hyphae and hyphae in the dissepiments with small rod-like crystals, pore surface straw-coloured to pale orange brown when dry $ C. gilvescens
4,5 $ Basidiospores ellipsoid 2.5-3.5 µm wide, basal hyphae smooth, pore surface whitish to pale cream when dry
5,0 $ Basidiospores 4-5 x 2.8-3.5 µm $ C. balaenae
5,0 $ Basidiospores 3-4 X 2.5-3 µm $ C. consobrina
6,0 $ Basidiocarps with cream rhizomorphs, pores angular, 1-2 per mm $ C. cremea
6,7 $ Basidiocarps without cream rhizomorphs, pores round to angular, 1-4 per mm
7,0 $ Pores 3-4 per mm, pore surface reddish when dry, scattered intercalary skeletal hyphae in the subiculum $ C. subrufa
7,8 $ Pores 1-3(4) per mm, pore surface straw-coloured or resinous brown when dry, no intercalary sketetal hyphae present
8,0 $ Basidiospores subcylindrical, 2-3 µm wide, pore surface totally or partly resinous brown, pores 2-3 (4) per mm, microscopical preparations with numerous globules, basal hyphae thickwalled $ C. resinascens
8,0 $ Basidiospores ellipsoid, 3.5-5 µm wide, pore surface cream to straw-coloured, pores 1-3 per mm, no globules present in microscopical preparations, all hyphae equally thin-walled $ C. aneirina
